    <decisions>
        <name>Is_Reminder_Due</name>
        <label>Is Reminder Due</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Not Due Yet</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Reminder_Due</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>DaysSinceLastEmail</leftValueReference>
                <operator>GreaterThanOrEqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <numberValue>2.0</numberValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>DaysSinceSentToBank</leftValueReference>
                <operator>LessThanOrEqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <numberValue>7.0</numberValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.ContactEmail__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsBlank</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Send_Pending_Signature_Reminder</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Reminder Due</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Resends the Pending Customer Signature email template every 2 days while a UAEDDS mandate is still awaiting signature, and stops once the mandate is 7 days past Sent To Bank. UAEDDS ages an unsigned mandate out to RQXP after 7 working days and the status poller turns that into Discarded, so chasing beyond day 7 can only email a customer about a mandate the bank has already abandoned. Runs daily and decides per record rather than being scheduled every 2 days, so a mandate that turns Pending on any day of the week is still chased on its own day 2.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <description>Whole days since the last Pending Customer Signature email. 999 when nothing has been stamped, so a mandate the record-triggered flow never emailed - one that was already Pending when this went live - still gets chased. Compared as dates rather than as a DateTime difference so the reminder lands on day 2 whatever time of day the first email went out.</description>
        <name>DaysSinceLastEmail</name>
        <dataType>Number</dataType>
        <expression>IF(
  ISBLANK({!$Record.Pending_Signature_Email_Sent_Date__c}),
  999,
  TODAY() - DATEVALUE({!$Record.Pending_Signature_Email_Sent_Date__c})
)</expression>
        <scale>0</scale>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>Days since the mandate went to UAEDDS. Sent_To_Bank_Date__c is the vendor signing clock, stamped by UAEDDS_MandateService.createMandate on the same update that sets this status, and never moved afterwards.</description>
        <name>DaysSinceSentToBank</name>
        <dataType>Number</dataType>
        <expression>TODAY() - {!$Record.Sent_To_Bank_Date__c}</expression>
        <scale>0</scale>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>EmailSentDateTime</name>
        <dataType>DateTime</dataType>
        <expression>NOW()</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>Treats a blank count as zero, so a mandate that was already Pending before this automation went live starts counting from 1 rather than staying blank.</description>
        <name>NextEmailCount</name>
        <dataType>Number</dataType>
        <expression>IF(
  ISBLANK({!$Record.Pending_Signature_Email_Count__c}),
  0,
  {!$Record.Pending_Signature_Email_Count__c}
) + 1</expression>
        <scale>0</scale>
    </formulas>
